      ],
      "description": "The dak vocabulary in code: `dak-blocks.ts` (the block builders `content-adapters/dak.json` names), `dak-kinds.ts` and `dak-jsonld.ts` (read off `block-kinds/`), `dak-content-type.ts`, `dak.ts`, and the l2-dak-authoring skill's input/output JSON Schemas. Declared at the cutover (bean hupw) so a remote mount brings it: the mounted adapter and QA checkers name these modules. It also holds the `schemas` graph, declared on 2026-10-26: until then it was found only by the schema reader's conventional fallback to `<instance>/schemas/`, which applies only while NO directory of the `schemas` kind exists among the instances stacked on smart-base. cat-harness's `ns/` (`cat-harness-ns`, kind `schemas`) is reproduced into every dependent, so the moment `jsonld:contexts` writes `ns/context/v1.jsonld` into an instance stacked on this one the fallback stopped and smart-base's schema fields left the extracted glossary, making `check:glossary` pass or fail on the order earlier writers ran in.",
      "fileCount": 0,
      "inSubgraph": "http://smart.who.int/base/directory/smart-base-schemas"
    }
  ]
